# .antigravityrules — vkon.in

Rules derived by inspecting this repository. Everything below reflects code that
exists today. Where a rule encodes a bug that has already happened, it says so.

> **Read first:** `AGENTS.md` (loaded via `CLAUDE.md`), then `docs/HANDOFF.md`,
> `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` and — for `/admin` work — `docs/ADMIN.md`. This file
> summarises; those are the authority.
>
> In `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` specifically: **§8** is the data model (four tables,
> per-column), **§8a** is the server surface (every route handler and server
> action with its signature, plus how data reaches the UI), and **§9** is the
> load-bearing constraints — each one encodes a bug that has already happened.
> There is deliberately **no second architecture document in the repo root**; a
> duplicate was folded into `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` on 2026-09-03 precisely so the
> two could not drift.

