## 2. Code standards

### Extensions and file naming
| Thing | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Component | `PascalCase.tsx` | `components/product/ProductCard.tsx` |
| Hook / client util | `camelCase.ts` | `components/cart/useCart.ts` |
| Library module | `camelCase.ts` | `lib/db/products.ts`, `lib/rate-limit.ts` |
| Route file | Next.js reserved lowercase | `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `route.ts` |
| Server actions | `actions.ts` co-located with its route group | `app/(site)/actions.ts` |
| Schema | `.sql` | `lib/db/schema.sql` |
| Node scripts | `.mjs` | `scripts/db-setup.mjs` |

`kebab-case.ts` appears only where the name is genuinely two words describing a
mechanism (`rate-limit.ts`). Prefer `camelCase.ts` for new lib modules.

### Imports
- Always use the `@/*` alias (`@/components/...`, `@/lib/...`, `@/content/...`).
  Relative imports appear only for same-directory siblings.
- Import order as found: external → `@/components` → `@/content` → `@/lib` →
  `import type`.
- Use `import type { … }` for type-only imports (`isolatedModules` is on).

### Components
- **Server component by default.** Add `"use client"` only for state, refs,
  effects, browser APIs, or event handlers. 36 of 46 components are client
  components; each one is listed with its justification in
  `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` → Client components. **Add your new client component to
  that table in the same change.**
- One component per file; the default export matches the filename. Small private
  sub-components may live in the same file below the main export (see
  `ProductCard.tsx`'s `HorizontalCard` / `FeaturedCard`).
- Props are declared inline as a destructured object with an inline type
  literal, not a separate `Props` interface:
  ```tsx
  export function ProductPrice({
    product,
    size = "compact",
  }: {
    product: Pick<Product, "price" | "discountPercent">;
    size?: "compact" | "regular";
  }) { … }
  ```
- Data is read in server components / route files and passed down. **Components
  never touch the database** — that is the layering rule below.

### Styling
- Tailwind utility classes inline. No CSS modules, no styled-components.
- **Use the semantic tokens** (`text-ink`, `bg-surface`, `border-line`,
  `text-accent`, `text-band-ink`, `text-price-off`, …), not raw palette values
  and not arbitrary hex. Dark mode works *because* only semantic tokens are
  redefined under `[data-theme="dark"]`.
- New colour → add it as a semantic token in **both** theme blocks in
  `globals.css`, and **state the measured contrast ratio in a comment**. Every
  pair in that file is measured and clears WCAG AA; that is a documented rule,
  not a habit.
- Shared multi-property idioms belong in `@layer components` / `@layer
  utilities` in `globals.css` (`.label-tech`, `.hscroll`, `.reveal`, `.tilt`,
  `.rule-grid`).
- Some named Tailwind utilities are **silently absent in this version** —
  `translate-x-1` and `scale-x-0` among them. The codebase uses the
  arbitrary-property form instead: `[transform:translateX(0.25rem)]`,
  `[transform:scaleX(0)]`. Follow that; a silent no-op has bitten this repo
  more than once.
- Tailwind v4 arbitrary values need underscores for spaces:
  `top-[min(0px,calc(100svh_-_38rem))]`.

### Comments
This codebase comments **why**, at length, and that is deliberate — comments
record decisions, rejected alternatives and the bug each constraint prevents.
Match that density when touching commented code. Do not delete a comment that
explains a constraint because the code around it moved.

